From 6909c31219fca44326da300a9330ffaf23f9830f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 03:53:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] draw/sw: never blend outside the target buffer

lv_draw_sw_blend() clips the blend area only to the task's clip area and
then asks for the start pixel with lv_draw_layer_go_to_xy(). When a clip
area reaches past the layer's buffer, an area left of or above the
buffer returns NULL and the blend writes through it; an area that only
overhangs to the right or bottom writes past the row or the buffer.

AERA reaches this with LV_DRAW_TRANSFORM_USE_MATRIX 1:
refr_obj_matrix() widens the clip area by the inverse of an object's
transform, which the SW renderer never applies. A Recents card or a
tile row that runs past a screen edge while shrunk on press, redrawn in
full (opening Recents, rotating), crashed recovery with SIGSEGV in
lv_draw_sw_blend.

Clip to the layer's buf_area as well, so a too-wide clip area costs a
skipped draw instead of a crash or memory corruption. Nothing else
changes: transforms stay drawn at 100% as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J6XhHxrkhAcXmkzHMeCnVz
---
 src/draw/sw/blend/lv_draw_sw_blend.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/draw/sw/blend/lv_draw_sw_blend.c b/src/draw/sw/blend/lv_draw_sw_blend.c
index 54a7294ac..7ee236c5b 100644
--- a/src/draw/sw/blend/lv_draw_sw_blend.c
+++ b/src/draw/sw/blend/lv_draw_sw_blend.c
@@ -79,8 +79,11 @@ void lv_draw_sw_blend(lv_draw_task_t * t, const lv_draw_sw_blend_dsc_t * blend_d
     lv_area_t blend_area;
     if(!lv_area_intersect(&blend_area, blend_dsc->blend_area, &t->clip_area)) return;
 
-    LV_PROFILER_DRAW_BEGIN;
+    /*Never write outside the target buffer, even if the clip area reaches past it*/
     lv_layer_t * layer = t->target_layer;
+    if(!lv_area_intersect(&blend_area, &blend_area, &layer->buf_area)) return;
+
+    LV_PROFILER_DRAW_BEGIN;
     uint32_t layer_stride_byte = layer->draw_buf->header.stride;
 
     lv_draw_sw_blend_handler_t handler = lv_draw_sw_get_blend_handler(layer->color_format);
